//
// A NON-PUB METHOD IS REFUSED FROM OUTSIDE ITS LIBRARY, HOWEVER IT IS REACHED (`@FR-F-Surface`).
// A library's surface is its `pub` items: a method without `pub` is refused to a consumer through
// the library's qualifier and on the library's own record type alike — the receiver's type being
// the library's grants nothing.  Each section is one refused call with its expectation and
// receipt.  A non-pub FUNCTION is refused one compile pass earlier, which a file with these never
// reaches: it is `a-non-pub-function-is-refused-through-the-qualifier.loft`.
//
// ── a-non-pub-method-is-refused-through-the-qualifier ──
//
// A NON-PUB METHOD IS REFUSED THROUGH THE QUALIFIER (`@FR-F-Surface`; found walking its pair with
// `@FR-Disp-Trigger`, whose triggers derive only from the pub surface).  `fn fs_tm(self: text)`
// is declared without `pub`, so `f_surface_fixture_lib::fs_tm("hi")` is an outside reach of a
// non-pub item and must be refused exactly as the non-pub plain function is.
//
// Guards loft#2115: the call was accepted and printed "hi." on both backends — a qualified call
// asked the library for the item by NAME, and a method is keyed by its receiver.  The method
// spelling on the library's own record is the cell beside this one.
//
// @falsified-at: e71f24b34 — accepted there (prints "hi."), interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile (the expected diagnostic).
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the item and the library.
// HOLDS: `a-non-pub-function-is-refused-through-the-qualifier` beside it.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `fs_tm` is not `pub` in `f_surface_fixture_lib`
//
// ── a-non-pub-method-is-refused-on-the-librarys-own-record ──
//
// A NON-PUB METHOD IS REFUSED ON THE LIBRARY'S OWN RECORD (`@FR-F-Surface`).  `fn fs_rm(self: FsP)`
// is declared without `pub`; a program holding a pub `FsP` reaches only the surface, so
// `p.fs_rm()` must be refused — the method spelling is a reach of the item like the qualifier.
//
// Guards loft#2115: accepted there and printed 7 on both backends (FsP{4}.x + 3) — the method
// spelling finds every method of the receiver type, and nothing asked its `pub`.
//
// @falsified-at: e71f24b34 — accepted there (prints 7), interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile (the expected diagnostic).
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the item and the library.
// HOLDS: `a-non-pub-function-is-refused-through-the-qualifier` beside it.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: fs_rm

use f_surface_fixture_lib::*;

fn test_a_non_pub_method_is_refused_through_the_qualifier() {
  println(f_surface_fixture_lib::fs_tm("hi"));
}


fn test_a_non_pub_method_is_refused_on_the_librarys_own_record() {
  p = FsP { x: 4 };
  println("{p.fs_rm()}");
}
